<rules>
{{- if .commands}}
- Use run for file operations, with Host's calls{{if .cosmic}} and cosmic's modules{{end}}; Host.bash runs a program where one is needed{{if .cosmic}}, and cosmic's own commands are there to run (cosmic test, cosmic fix --check, cosmic uses, cosmic docs): start with them, not with ls, cat or git status{{end}}
{{- else if .run}}
- Use run for file operations: no program runs here, so do with Host's calls{{if .cosmic}} and cosmic's modules{{end}} what a command would
{{- end}}
{{- with .tools}}{{range .}}{{range .guidelines}}
- {{.}}
{{- end}}{{end}}{{end}}
{{- if .tree}}
- A snippet requires the working directory's own modules as a file there does: require("util") reads util.tl and checks it with the snippet, so require a file you wrote to run and check it
{{- end}}
- Tools may run in a sandbox: where one is refused (a read-only file system, a path not there, no network), say so rather than working around it.
{{- if .commands}}
- Check a change with the project's own checks and tests (Host.bash) before calling it done, and say what you ran.
{{- else}}
- No program runs here, so the project's own tests cannot: say a change is unchecked by them.
{{- end}}
- Be concise in your responses
- Show file paths clearly when working with files
</rules>
